---
import "../styles/global.css";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy - Striff" description="How Striff collects, uses and protects your information." canonical="https://striff.io/privacy">
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-20">
    <h1 class="mb-8 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">Privacy Policy</h1>

    <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
      <p class="text-slate-600">Last updated: October 2, 2026</p>

      <p class="mt-4">Striff is operated by HADI Technology ("we", "us"), a Canadian corporation. This policy covers the striff.io website, the Striff GitHub App and dashboard, and the Striffs for GitHub browser extension.</p>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">1. Information We Collect</h2>
        <ul class="ml-6 list-disc">
          <li><strong>Website usage</strong>: pages visited, browser and device type, referring website and approximate location, collected through cookies and analytics.</li>
          <li><strong>Messages</strong>: what you send us through the contact form or by email.</li>
          <li><strong>Account information</strong>: when you sign in with GitHub, your GitHub username, account ID, email address and organization membership.</li>
          <li><strong>Billing information</strong>: your plan and subscription status. Payments are handled by our payment processor; we do not receive your card details.</li>
          <li><strong>Repository information</strong>: the repository content and pull request information Striff needs to analyse a change, including the GitHub usernames of pull request authors, and the results Striff produces from it. Source code is not retained after an analysis.</li>
          <li><strong>Browser extension</strong>: an optional GitHub token, stored only in your browser, and anonymous usage events.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">2. How We Use It</h2>
        <p>To provide and secure Striff, bill for it, communicate with you about your account and requests, and improve it. We do not sell personal information, use it for advertising, or use your code or documentation to train AI models.</p>
        <p class="mt-2">Where EU or UK data protection law applies, we rely on performing our contract with you, our legitimate interests in operating, securing and improving Striff, your consent for analytics cookies, and our legal obligations for billing records.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">3. Sharing</h2>
        <p>We share information only with GitHub, as part of providing the service, and with service providers that process it on our behalf: hosting, AI processing, payments, email delivery, error monitoring and analytics. We may also disclose information when required by law, or as part of a merger or acquisition.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">4. Where It Is Processed</h2>
        <p>Our servers are in Canada. Our service providers may process information in other countries, including the United States, where it may be accessible to authorities under local law.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">5. Retention</h2>
        <p>We keep information for as long as we need it to provide Striff to you, and delete it on request or when it is no longer needed, except where the law requires us to keep it, such as billing records.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">6. Security</h2>
        <p>We use reasonable technical and organizational safeguards to protect your information, including encryption in transit.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">7. Your Rights</h2>
        <p>You can ask to access, correct or delete your personal information, or withdraw your consent, by emailing <a href="mailto:hi@haditechnology.com" class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-700">hi@haditechnology.com</a>. You may also complain to the Office of the Privacy Commissioner of Canada or, in the EU, the UK or elsewhere, to your local data protection authority.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">8. Cookies</h2>
        <p>See our <a href="/cookies" class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-700">Cookie Policy</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">9. Children</h2>
        <p>Striff is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect their information.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">10. Changes</h2>
        <p>We may update this policy and will post any changes on this page with a new "Last updated" date.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">11. Contact</h2>
        <p>For privacy questions, email <a href="mailto:hi@haditechnology.com" class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-700">hi@haditechnology.com</a>.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
